{"type": "model", "t_ms": 180932, "ts": 1795232951.4577398, "turn": 4, "prompt_tokens": 8093, "completion_tokens": 1718, "finish_reason": "stop", "reasoning_tokens": null, "ttft_ms": 3065, "latency_ms": 58494, "usage_source": "reported", "cache_hit_tokens": null, "cache_miss_tokens": null, "error": "", "text": "{\"thought\": \"The result is not the flag. The encryption does c = pow(c,e,n) three times sequentially, so c = m^(e^3) mod n1, mod n2, mod n3. But the final c is only reduced mod n3 (the last). So c = m^(e^3) mod n3. I should decrypt using n3, not n1. Let me use n3.\", \"action\": \"python\", \"code\": \"from Crypto.Util.number import long_to_bytes\\\\\\\\ne=65537\\\\nn3=q*r\\nphi=(q-1)*(r-1)\\nd=pow(e**3, -1, phi)\\nm=pow(c, d, n3)\\nprint(long_to_bytes(m))\"}"}
